3. Today's Mini Project — Account Risk Automation | 25 min

Now you code.

Requirement:

> Whenever an Opportunity changes to Closed Won, update its related Account's Customer_Status__c to Active.



But your solution must support 200 Opportunities simultaneously.

Requirements:

No SOQL inside loop
No DML inside loop
Use Trigger.oldMap
Use Set
Use Trigger Handler
Perform only necessary updates

Structure:

OpportunityTrigger
        ↓
OpportunityTriggerHandler
        ↓
detect Stage change
        ↓
collect Account IDs
        ↓
update Accounts

Expected files

force-app/
└── main/
    └── default/
        ├── triggers/
        │   └── OpportunityTrigger.trigger
        └── classes/
            ├── OpportunityTriggerHandler.cls
            └── OpportunityTriggerHandlerTest.cls

Bonus challenge:

Write a test that creates:

1 Account
↓
5 Opportunities
↓
update all 5 → Closed Won
↓
Account should become Active

Use:

Test.startTest();

update opportunities;

Test.stopTest();

Then:

System.assertEquals(
    'Active',
    updatedAccount.Customer_Status__c
);

Don't worry about making it perfect on the first attempt. The important part is that you write it yourself.


