4. Git/GitHub — Feature Branch Workflow | 10 min

For your switch, I want you comfortable explaining Git instead of only saying “I've used Git.”

Imagine ticket:

SF-1023
Opportunity Account Status Automation

Create branch:

git checkout main
git pull
git checkout -b feature/SF-1023-opportunity-status

After coding:

git status

Stage:

git add .

Commit:

git commit -m "SF-1023 Add Opportunity account status automation"

Push:

git push -u origin feature/SF-1023-opportunity-status

Then create PR:

feature/SF-1023-opportunity-status
            ↓
           main

A CI/CD pipeline—Harness, GitHub Actions, Jenkins, etc.—can then run validation/tests before deployment.

Your experience with Git branching, PRs, CI/CD and Salesforce deployments is already on your resume, so later sessions will turn this into proper interview-level DevOps knowledge rather than just command memorisation.


